{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310705,"nonce":"sC+C5FAKORrbP3wizy6kv+EsYZ0=","title":"FIXED 2026-09-05 (phi-SRA seeded fields by BLOCK-ID order; 9-line repro R8). Was: OPEN (20-line repro `kvtwin`): a user class holding an ...","message":"`scalar_replacement.rs` `try_build_phi_candidate` seeded each promoted field from the LAST store in\n`sorted_blocks` (block-id) order. The inliner (inlining.rs:843) inlines a block's call sites\nlast-first and moves the tail into a fresh continuation block, so an object allocated AFTER an\ninlinable call has its zero-init in a HIGHER block than the ctor's real store ⇒ the null zero-init\nwon ⇒ `%9 = phi ptr [null, …]`. 9-line repro R8: `var sm = new SM(); var it = new KV(); it.m = sm;\nwhile (n \u003c it.m.c) n++;` (SIGILL); swap the two `new` lines ⇒ passes. FIX: `reaching_field_stores`\nwalks the unconditional-branch chain from the allocating block to the edge's source block, records\nstores in execution order, and REFUSES the candidate on any branch. Companion (S9): the phi-SRA\nescape scan ignored StoreGlobal/CallIndirect uses ⇒ `static keep = it` deleted the alloc; now any\nother reader of a tracked value refuses the candidate.\nSWITCHES THAT WORK UNDER `rayzor run` (memory saying bundle-only was STALE): `RAYZOR_NO_PHI_SRA=1`,\n`RAYZOR_NO_SRA=1`, `RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES=scalar_replacement|inlining|dead-code-elimination`.\nRegular `apply_sra` already used `bfs_block_order`; only the phi path had the id-order heuristic.\n\n**Repro** (`$SP/kvtwin/Main.hx`): `interface IM\u003cK,V\u003e{get;keys}`, `class KV\u003cK,V\u003e{var m:IM\u003cK,V\u003e; var ks:Iterator\u003cK\u003e; new(m){this.m=m; ks=m.keys();} hasNext(){return ks.hasNext();}}`,\n`class SM implements IM\u003cString,Int\u003e` over a StringMap; `main(){ var it = new KV(sm); while(it.hasNext())… }` ⇒ `n=0`.\nPre-opt LLVM IR of `main`: the interface call `%26 = call ptr %22(env, obj)` is emitted, but the KV\nobject's fields are `%9 = phi ptr [null, %27]`, `%10 = phi ptr [null, %27]` — the inlined\nconstructor's field stores are gone. Moving `new KV(sm)` into `static function mk(sm)` ⇒ MATCH.\nNot the devirtualizer (fixed separately, [[bugs-devirtualizer-dropped-closure-env]]) and not the\ninterface path (kvtwin3 proves it). This is the \"SRA drops inlined ctor stores\" item.\n\n**How to apply:** when an interface/handle probe reads back NULL fields, first move construction\ninto a helper; if that fixes it, it is this defect, not dispatch. Bisect with\n`RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES` (bundle only) per [[bugs-mir-local-scan-global-conclusion]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_sra_drops_inlined_ctor_field_stores` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}